      <h2 class="section-title" style="color: #FFFFFF; font-size: clamp(1.85rem, 2.6vw, 2.5rem); margin-bottom: 12px; line-height: 1.25;">
        Environmentally Friendly Packaging Solutions for <br>
        <span style="color: #34D399;">Hazardous & Non-Hazardous Products</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="section-subtitle" style="color: #CBD5E1; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.65;">
        Parth Packaging operates under statutory authorization from the <strong>Maharashtra Pollution Control Board (MPCB)</strong> (Consent No. <code>MPCB/RO(HQ)/HSMD/Amendment/P-31</code>), certified under the Water Act 1974, Air Act 1981, and Hazardous Waste Management Rules. Authorized to decontaminate and recondition up to 4,800 drums/month with 100% closed-loop ETP water recycling.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 0.85fr; gap: 36px; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
      <!-- HOW IT IS ENVIRONMENT FRIENDLY (Kaise Environment Friendly Hai) -->
      <div>
        <h3 style="color: #FFFFFF; font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 16px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;">
          <span>🌱</span> How Our Reconditioning Protects the Environment:
        </h3>

        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px;">
          <!-- Pillar 1: Carbon Reduction -->
          <div style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 4px solid #10B981; border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px 18px;">
            <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 4px;">
              <h4 style="color: #FFFFFF; font-size: 1rem; margin: 0; font-weight: 700;">1. 72% Carbon Footprint Reduction (18.4 kg CO2e Saved / Drum)</h4>
              <span style="background: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.2); color: #34D399; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 700; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 4px;">Decarbonization</span>
            </div>
            <p style="color: #94A3B8; font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0;">
              Synthesizing new virgin high-density polyethylene (HDPE) requires extensive fossil fuel extraction, emitting ~25.6 kg CO2e per drum. Reconditioning emits only 7.2 kg CO2e—cutting greenhouse emissions by 72% and helping client enterprises achieve corporate Scope 3 net-zero targets.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Pillar 2: Landfill Diversion -->
          <div style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 4px solid #38BDF8; border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px 18px;">
            <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 4px;">
              <h4 style="color: #FFFFFF; font-size: 1rem; margin: 0; font-weight: 700;">2. 10.5 kg Heavy Polymer Diverted from Landfills per Unit</h4>
              <span style="background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.2); color: #38BDF8; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 700; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 4px;">Zero Landfill</span>
            </div>
            <p style="color: #94A3B8; font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0;">
              Industrial rigid polymers take over 450 years to degrade. Reconditioning restores containers to certified structural standards across multiple industrial turns, diverting thousands of tons of rigid plastic from open dumps and municipal landfills.
